{
  "format": "misaka.palw.model-adapter.v1",
  "id": "gemma4-text",
  "doc": "Gemma-4's text decoder: Gemma's four RMSNorms around the mixer and the FFN (plain gains), the per-layer input (PLE) and a learned layer scalar; per-head QK-norm with gains and a weightless V-norm at scale 1; sliding layers with the default rope, full layers with their own head width and KV heads (per_layer_config, or global_head_dim / num_global_key_value_heads) and the proportional rope; with attention_k_eq_v the full layers' values are the raw key projection; the last num_kv_shared_layers layers reuse the keys and values of the last earlier layer of their own type (double-wide MLP with use_double_wide_mlp); with enable_moe_block a softmax top-k MoE runs beside the MLP.",
